sec.p:
Our macroscopic model is designed to test whether clonal interference alone can prevent selective sweeps and to obtain upper bounds on selective sweep probabilities during range expansions. We consider a wildtype population that starts expanding spherically at time t = 0, such that its radius xwt grows at speed cwt. Focusing on selective sweeps, we consider only advantageous mutations, which we assume spread within the wildtype at speed cm > cwt (Fig. 1). Mutations occur at per-capita rate \documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
