				\begin{document}$$c=2\sqrt{aD}$$\end{document}c=2aD, where D is the diffusion coefficient carrying information of migration and a is the difference in the local proliferation rate. More recent studies have sought to refine and generalise this result44–47. Our main results apply to any model that generates approximately constant speeds.

